00:02:59.849 --> 00:03:02.840
Alright Hank, here's the last thing I want
to say about Nerdfighting and civility. No

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:08.379
one can tell you if you're a Nerdfighter and
you can't tell anyone else if they're a Nerdfighter.

00:03:08.379 --> 00:03:12.849
Nerdfighter is an identity that you choose
and then we collectively define that identity.

00:03:12.849 --> 00:03:16.970
Not by talking about what it means, but by
living it. And in my opinion that goes for

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:21.390
almost all identities, from the ones we choose
like musician or writer, to the ones that

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:23.400
seem unchosen like brother.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:27.650
Identities are important, but both the ones
you choose and the ones that choose you generally

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:31.390
resist simple definitions. I mean Hank, if
I've learned anything about brotherhood in

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:35.650
